WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.150
There are thousands of refugees entering
Bangladesh every day. They cross the

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.510
border of Myanmar where the state
military has launched a violent

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:14.070
offensive against an ethnic minority
group – the Rohingya. The UN reported

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:19.560
that since August 2017 about 400,000
Rohingya men women and children have

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.580
fled their homes in Myanmar's Rakhine
State. Reports claimed that the military

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.810
has been killing and raping the Rohingya
and has set their villages on fire.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:33.210
Satellite imagery showing burned
villages confirms those reports.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:38.070
Because Myanmar has refused access to human rights investigators, the current

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:44.270
situation cannot yet be fully assessed
but the situation remains or seems a

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:49.410
textbook example of ethnic
cleansing. The term ethnic cleansing has

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.879
been reserved for some of the worst
atrocities in history. The UN defines it

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:59.160
as a purposeful policy designed by one
ethnic or religious group to remove by

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:04.170
violent and terror inspiring means the
civilian population of another ethnic or

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.780
religious group from certain geographic
areas.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.740
What makes Myanmar a textbook example is that the military has been launching

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.150
attacks on the Rohingya – a Muslim
minority in a majority Buddhist country.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:19.259
Violent tactics have forced tens of
thousands of Rohingya to flee their

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:24.119
homes. While many fled to Malaysia and
Thailand most ended up in Bangladesh.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:28.259
The recent wave of violence is the latest in a pattern of discrimination that started

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:35.159
over 50 years ago. In 1962, Myanmar –
then called Burma – was taken over by the

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:39.299
military in a coup. They got rid of the
country's constitution and created a

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.799
military junta. Like many dictatorships
they promoted fierce nationalism based

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:47.369
on the country's Buddhist identity and
when they needed a common enemy to help

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:52.320
unite the population the Rohingya were
singled out as a threat. Tensions between

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.189
the Burmese Buddhist population and the
Rohingya go back to the Second World War

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:00.180
when each group supported opposing sides. The Rohingya sided with the British

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.439
colonialists who ruled the country and
the Buddhists mostly sided with the

00:02:04.439 --> 00:02:08.849
Japanese invaders hoping they'd help end
the British rule after the war. But even

00:02:08.849 --> 00:02:12.690
in modern Myanmar the Rohingya
minority continued to be an easy target.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.350
Although their lineage can be traced
back to 15th century Burma, the

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:20.070
government has been forcing them out
claiming their illegal immigrants from

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:24.000
Bangladesh.
It started in 1978 after a massive

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.190
crackdown called Operation Dragon King
forced about 200,000 Rohingya to flee to

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:33.600
Bangladesh. The military reportedly used
violence and rape to drive them out.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.190
About a hundred and seventy thousand Rohingya reportedly returned to Burma. Then

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:44.220
in 1982, the government passed the
Citizenship Act recognizing 135 ethnic

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.900
groups. The Rohingya, with a population
of about 1 million, were not on the list

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:54.270
and became a stateless people. In 1991,
Myanmar's military launched another

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:58.920
campaign literally called "Operation
clean and beautiful nation." This time

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.770
about 250,000 Rohingya fled to
Bangladesh. Tensions continued to build

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:08.700
against the Rohingya in the 2000s. Violence broke out in 2012

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.660
when four Muslim men were accused of
raping and killing a buddhist woman in

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.530
Rakhine. Buddhist nationalist backed by
security forces attacked Muslim

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:20.550
neighborhoods, burned homes displacing
tens of thousands of Rohingya again.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:25.500
Human Rights Watch deemed it an ethnic
cleansing campaign. By this point the

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:31.140
Rohingya were persecuted
disenfranchised and stateless. In 2016, a

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:35.520
Rohingya militant group, the Arakan Rohingya Salvation Army, emerged and

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.750
coordinated small-scale attacks on
border police stations. An attack on

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:45.959
August 25th 2017 left 12 police officers
dead and sparked the current crisis

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:50.280
against Rohingya civilians. A brutal
retaliation by the state security forces

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:56.519
has led to about 400 deaths and the mass
exodus of about 400,000 Rohingya to

00:03:56.519 --> 00:04:01.530
Bangladesh. Since the August attack 210
villages have been burned to the ground.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.820
The violent campaign has triggered the
fastest growing humanitarian crisis in

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:10.200
recent years, but Myanmar's de facto
leader and Nobel Peace Prize winner

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.250
Aung San Suu Ky has barely acknowledged the attacks.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:21.959
More than 50% of the villages of Muslims
are intact they are as they were before

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:27.630
the attacks took place. When she says
that, you know, 50% of the Muslim villages

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:32.310
are still present in Rakhine State wel,l
I mean, what are we talking about? 50% are

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.490
gone. 50% are burnt out. You know in any school

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:40.200
I went to 50% is a failing grade. Recent
reports claimed that the military has

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.280
planted landmines along the Bangladesh
border to prevent the Rohingya from

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.550
returning. Myanmar's government has systematically

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:51.720
driven the Rohingya out of the country.
Over the last five decades it has

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.970
stripped their citizenship, terrorized
them, and destroyed their homes, and now

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:14.230
it wants to keep them from ever coming
back.

